  "curriculum": "The 2026–2027 regulations identify the full-time 180 EC Medicine bachelor (ISAT 56551). Articles 4.1 and 7.1 set annual totals of 60 EC. Shared Causes of Diseases modules and cumulative Knowledge Development sit alongside longitudinal Competency Development. Sustainable Care is the first-listed of four communities for the same competency slots, with no general route designated. The official ordering resolves the tie independently of UCR. The public programme page describes Dutch instruction for new entrants. Transitional rules for the former English route do not define the current entrant curriculum. No free-choice minor is added.",
  "progression": "Article 5.2 normally requires 45 first-year credits for positive binding study advice. Article 6.1 requires meeting that threshold for year two and completing all 60 first-year credits for year three under ordinary progression. Article 9.3 sequences Knowledge Development B1 to B2 to B3, Competency Development 1.1 to 2.1 to 3.1 and 1.2 to 2.2, with both 2.2 and 3.1 required before 3.2. The July study guide pp. 36–38 adds the approved proposal requirement. Research is undertaken in teams of three to five with individual work and assessment in the 20 EC final competency block. The UCR optional element is a separately displayed 15 EC opportunity and outside all 180 EC schedules.",
